course: dictionary
lesson: 15723
title: Calm and quiet: tranquillity
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tranquillity is a calm, quiet, peaceful state, with no noise, hurry or worry. Writers use it to paint peaceful places. «We sat by the lake at dawn, enjoying the tranquillity of the still water.» Nothing is rushing or shouting here, so tranquillity must mean peace and quiet.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «The sudden bang shattered the tranquillity of the garden.» A sudden bang is loud and unexpected, and shattered means broken. So the tranquillity was calm before the bang, and now it is gone.
explain: Tranquillity can also be a feeling inside a person. «Sam felt a sense of tranquillity after his deep breaths.» Sam is not in a quiet place, but he feels calm inside, so the word describes his mind as well as his surroundings.
fact: Tranquillity is a noun. It means a calm, quiet, peaceful state.
fact: «Tranquillity» means calm and peaceful, with no noise, hurry or worry.
fact: A person can feel tranquillity inside, as well as a place having it.
fact: In American spelling, the word is tranquility.
fact: The Moon has a «Sea of Tranquillity», where the first people landed in 1969.
exercise: «We sat by the lake at dawn, enjoying the tranquillity of the still water.» What does tranquillity mean here? | *Calm and peaceful quiet | Cold and wet weather | Fast and hurried movement | Loud and busy noise
exercise: «The sudden bang shattered the tranquillity of the garden.» What does this sentence show? | *The peace of the garden was broken | The birds were fed | The garden was made bigger | The flowers were painted
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to tranquillity? | Worry | *Peace | Hurry | Noise
test: «Sam felt a sense of tranquillity after his deep breaths.» Where is the tranquillity? | On the football pitch | *In his mind and feelings | In the garden | In a fast car
test: «The library was full of tranquillity; nobody spoke above a whisper.» What does the sentence tell you? | *The room was calm and quiet | The room was loud with music | The room was on fire | The room was full of runners
exam: Which phrase shows tranquillity best? | A crowded market at noon | A loud fire alarm in a school | *A still lake at dawn with no one about | A rushing train at rush hour
